   'It moves opaque bytes and dispatches on a path string, so there is no place a
    per-field cost could enter.' Checked rather than trusted:
   core/src/rpc.rs: 0 mentions of any message type in this schema
   ../rust/crates/rpc/src/lib.rs: 2 mentions of any message type in this schema

== the arm ==
grpc++ 1.51.1 server on 127.0.0.1:50077, in-process

Crossings per RPC: TWO, and it is a property of the code rather than a
measurement -- `ak_call_unary` in, `ak_bytes_free` out. The core's RPC module
names no message type anywhere, so there is no place a per-field cost could
enter; `gen/rpc.sh` greps for that rather than trusting this sentence.

